cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this measurement, please cite it as below."
title: "adsbdb / hexdb.io route accuracy: measured"
abstract: >-
  A measurement of how accurately free callsign-to-route lookup services resolve
  an aircraft's origin and destination, and of where that error actually lives.
  The failure is regional rather than a matter of database staleness: adsbdb is
  27% correct on US domestic flights and 79% correct across the other regions
  sampled, while record age barely matters. The US figure was independently
  replicated at 28.6% across 395 flights using filed FAA flight plans as the
  arbiter. Also measures a geometric plausibility check that rejects routes an
  aircraft's own position contradicts, validated on data it was not designed
  against.
